[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Intel optional-profile and complex-boundary qualification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MUT-OPTIONAL-PROFILE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bind optional-code mutation evidence to an enabled profile
STATEMENT: >>>
Mutation qualification of an optional backend shall execute that backend's
enabled feature and applicable provider tests. A selected mutation in disabled
code shall not be reported as evidence of equivalence or tested numerical
behavior. Separate profile outcomes shall retain original candidate identities.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Intel83 replay source d786a58, intel-opencl feature, trusted native
provider and lib/intel_backend/providers/campaign_cli. Original frozen outcomes
remain unchanged. Raw evidence: docs/intel-mutation-profile-results.md.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: INTEL-RELATIVE-BOUNDARY-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve scale-independent and inclusive residual acceptance
STATEMENT: >>>
Intel adapter verification shall reject a relative residual above 1e-10 even
when its absolute residual is small, accept finite valid solutions across
equation scales, and accept the represented 1e-10 boundary inclusively.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: backend_intel::tests::relative_residual_is_not_an_absolute_small_number_gate;
represented_relative_error_boundary_is_inclusive includes the adjacent-ULP
rejection. The fixtures verify the safe owned gate, not the native kernel.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: INTEL-COMPLEX-ADMISSION-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Independently validate and embed complex systems
STATEMENT: >>>
The Intel backend shall reject incompatible complex matrix/RHS dimensions or
either nonfinite RHS component as InvalidInput. One complex unknown shall map
to two real unknowns, and finite known complex solutions shall retain both
components. The backend shall retain its documented experimental identity.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: actual_intel_circuit_contract tests independent malformed inputs,
scalar A=.5+.25j with x=2-3j, and explicit backend name/capability identity.
Actual trusted provider execution is required; missing hardware is not a pass.
<<<
